note top of TDDTest
  <b>Test Class (RED Phase)</b>

  Tests are written FIRST, before implementation.
  Each test defines expected behavior:

  <b>Cycle 1:</b> Basic commission (10% rate)
  <b>Cycle 2:</b> Deal validation (CLOSED status)
  <b>Cycle 3:</b> Tiered rates (8%, 10%, 12%)
  <b>Cycle 4:</b> Bonus calculation (15% bonus)
  <b>Cycle 5:</b> Full pipeline integration
  <b>Cycle 6:</b> Edge cases and validation
  <b>Cycle 7:</b> Calculation tracking

  Tests drive the implementation!
end note

note bottom of TDD
  <b>Implementation Class (GREEN Phase)</b>

  Code written to make tests pass.
  Started simple, evolved through cycles:

  • Minimal code first (GREEN)
  • Refactored for quality (REFACTOR)
  • Added features incrementally
  • Tests guide design decisions

  <b>Key Features:</b>
  • Basic commission calculation
  • Deal eligibility validation
  • Progressive tier rates
  • Bonus application
  • Calculation tracking
  • Error handling
end note

note right of Deal
  <b>Domain Model</b>

