' TDD Example Flow
note as ExampleFlow
  <b>Example TDD Flow: Tiered Commission</b>

  <b>RED:</b> Write test for tiered rates
  @Test
  void testTieredCommission() {
    assertEquals(2400, // 8% of 30000
      service.calculateTiered(30000));
    assertEquals(7500, // 10% of 75000
      service.calculateTiered(75000));
    assertEquals(18000, // 12% of 150000
      service.calculateTiered(150000));
  }

  Result: ❌ FAIL (Method doesn't exist)

  <b>GREEN:</b> Implement tier logic
  public BigDecimal calculateTiered(BigDecimal value) {
    if (value <= 50000) return value * 0.08;
    if (value <= 100000) return value * 0.10;
    return value * 0.12;
  }

  Result: ✅ PASS

  <b>REFACTOR:</b> Extract magic numbers
  final BigDecimal TIER_1_MAX = new BigDecimal("50000");
  final BigDecimal TIER_1_RATE = new BigDecimal("0.08");
  // ... use constants instead of magic numbers

  Result: ✅ PASS (Tests still green!)
end note

